  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the probability that a randomly selected subset of the divisors of 2025 has the property that the least common multiple (LCM) of its elements is 2025. We will do this step by step.\n\n1. **Find the prime factorization of 2025:**\n   \\[\n   2025 = 3^4 \\times 5^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of divisors of 2025:**\n   The number of divisors of a number \\( n = p_1^{e_1} \\times p_2^{e_2} \\times \\cdots \\times p_k^{e_k} \\) is given by \\( (e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1) \\). For \\( 2025 = 3^4 \\times 5^2 \\):\n   \\[\n   (4 + 1)(2 + 1) = 5 \\times 3 = 15\n   \\]\n   So, there are 15 divisors of 2025.\n\n3. **Determine the subsets of the divisors:**\n   The total number of subsets of a set with 15 elements is \\( 2^{15} \\).\n\n4. **Determine the favorable subsets:**\n   For a subset of the divisors to have an LCM of 2025, it must include all the prime factors of 2025. The divisors of 2025 are:\n   \\[\n   1, 3, 5, 9, 15, 25, 27, 45, 75, 135, 225, 375, 675, 2025\n   \\]\n   A subset that has an LCM of 2025 must include the elements \\( 1, 3, 5, 9, 15, 25, 27, 45, 75, 135, 225, 375, 675, 2025 \\). The only subset of these divisors that includes all of them is the set itself, which has \\( 2^{15} \\) subsets (including the empty set).\n\n5. **Calculate the probability:**\n   The probability that a randomly selected subset of the divisors of 2025 has an LCM of 2025 is the number of favorable subsets divided by the total number of subsets:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2^{15} - 1}{2^{15}} = \\frac{32768 - 1}{32768} = \\frac{32767}{32768}\n   \\]\n   The fraction \\( \\frac{32767}{32768} \\) is in its simplest form, so \\( m = 32767 \\) and \\( n = 32768 \\).\n\n6. **Find \\( m + n \\):**\n   \\[\n   m + n = 32767 + 32768 = 65535\n   \\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{65535}\n\\]",
